 thereafter  from resurrection F and to an even  greater degree in Dragon Ball super as  I've said before one of Dragon Balls  biggest problems was Goku and the main  casts ever increasing power level  raising the stakes to ridiculous absurd  levels and while beerus his presence  does give goku a chance to be an  underdog in a fight he also provides a  massive downside that Dragon Ball and  Dragon Ball Z never once had to contend  with a loss of tension Dragon Ball Z is  one of those series that provided  countless nail-biting moments where we  were left on the edge of our collective  seats wondering if Goku is Vegeta if  tension on our room ever was going to  pull through that tension that suspense  is what made Dragon Ball so incredibly  compelling it's why when I pick up a  Dragon Ball manga and open a random page  I get sucked in so easily it always did  a terrific job of creating tension and  one way of breaking down tension sucking  the atmosphere out of a scene is like  this lots fearless that's not polite  freezer you forgot to say Lord now I can  understand that many fans of the beerus  character will offer the argument that  beerus really isn't on anyone's side  he tries to be neutral and really  wouldn't care too much it frees a  defeated Goku there and then but that's  sort of the problem that mentality  surrounding what should be the biggest  fight to date in the series makes  everything feel less important it makes  us think well what's the big deal about  watching the second best fight that can  happen and when your film and subsequent  television series doesn't pay off beerus  at all it makes me wonder what does he  offer this scene what value is he adding  and the answer is none well that's not  entirely true either but it did ruin the  flow of the film and the enjoyment of  the battle for a lot of people including  myself the fight scene takes up a large  chunk of the film and a massive turning  point narrative Lee within this movie  was how Frieza would react to Vegeta  being yet another obstacle to overcome  despite finishing Goku through clever  tactics imagine how suspenseful freezes  defeat of Goku would have been had  Vegeta being the only other person left  to settle things and imagine if we  didn't know if he even stood a chance  it's difficult now to look back at what  could have been but this for me is a  massive part of what made this movie  significantly worse than battle of gods  however with that said it's not like  beerus didn't to offer anything to the  film his presence in that scene offered  some levity through humor that only  someone like him with a far superior  power level could enjoy during climactic  scenes like this one however even with  the humor and light-hearted endearing  banter he expressed in the prior film in  this one it really starts to become a  tiring routine in resurrection F at  least for me  it became extremely obvious that the  writers felt obligated to include beerus  but didn't have the first idea of what  to do with him they needed Wiese as his  involvement was crucial for the film to  reach its conclusion but beerus was just  sort of there i mean if you really think  about it what changes if you remove  beerus from this equation not much and  unfortunately his involvement wasn't  without a massive drawback to the  overall atmosphere of the film and  scenes and it only got worse from here  a strength that beerus offered to battle  of gods was that he showed yet again  that there will always be someone  stronger than goku that concept works  fantastically well in a movie format  that lasts around two hours it's sort of  a natural extension of what Dragonball  and go whose philosophy has been  throughout the series but take that  concept and now stretched across a 131  episode long series and you get a  character that sucks the drama and  stakes out of every fight the main cast  is in and proves to be less and less  funny with the same style of jokes  popping up again again again now that's  not to say that I don't think beerus has  any funny moments at all in Dragon Ball  super again he has had some moments  where I got legitimately amused by him  but he honestly provides more misses  than hits when it comes to the comedy  section his presence largely serves only  to turn the spectacle of a massive  dragon ball fight into a couple of kids  having a scuffle while he the dad  watches from the park bench  he has great moments that exist within  the series itself and I will acknowledge  that wholeheartedly he's had some  brighter moments that have shown him  more interesting side to him on occasion  but again it's been more misses than  hits when you take into account the  entire series so in that lies and in  that vein I understand that people have  a distaste and are fed up with the  character despite having terrific  upsides early on and one of my favorite  designs for a character in the entire  show it's obvious that the talent behind  toys writing staff as well as a Keira  Toriyama really have nothing for him  while we wait for his inevitable rematch  against Goku and nothing demonstrates  that more clearly than the Broly film  they had nothing for this character they  needed Wiis involved and because these  two are sort of attached at the hip  beerus once again like in resurrection F  is forced into being involved  however unlike resurrection F they seem  to have learned from their past mistake  and sidelined the character almost  immediately after he showed his face  look my main issue with beerus isn't  necessarily his character i actually  really enjoy it  his personality is playful and  compliments Goku's in a fascinating way  that even Dragon Ball super has  demonstrated I love his design I love  the general theme of what he has going  on but strangely it's how he fits and  complements many aspects of modern  Dragonball that I really don't like tons  of folks complained over the lack of  tension in Dragon Ball super early on  and the two arcs that happen to have the  most tension were the ones that traveled  to the future without beerus involved  and the universe survival arc which  again beerus couldn't be involved with I  personally think we're at a point right  now where the next move for beerus is to  be lesser than Goku or Vegeta witnessing  how he reacts to this sudden shift in  status quo could be interesting and  offer a lot in the way of development  for him if that's the direction they so  choose but until then in my opinion  beerus is still something of a problem  character  thanks for watching  [Music]

